WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
A conversational way to explore automotive catalog data without writing SQL.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The real Windows prototype turns an OE-reference question into a catalog lookup.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
SQL Server returns the records. The interface exposes both a conversation and a results table.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.133
The follow-up returns vehicle applications. Part numbers, usernames, and vehicle-count values are blurred.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:37.000
The SQL view makes the proposal inspectable. The backend checks and normalizes it before execution.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:45.000
OpenAI proposes the query. SQL Server supplies the rows, which are formatted locally.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The public validator is adapted from the prototype. It checks parsed SQL syntax, rather than trusting the model.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Table references, syntax, and functions have explicit limits. Unsupported operations are rejected.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:14.000
ToArray completes validation for the whole plan before the executor is called.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:23.000
If a later query is rejected, earlier queries in the same plan must not run either.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:33.000
This public test supplies a rejected second query, then asserts that the executor was called zero times.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:41.000
All 105 public test cases passed in this run. Passing tests does not prove every AI-generated answer is correct.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:53.000
The public sample is runnable without company access. Its planner is offline and all catalog records are fictional.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Working prototype · Public source and tests · Browser demo with fictional data
